nt_coverage":null,"_score_int_coverage":null,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":0.0005897796336875181,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":28.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":2.1437775545849265,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.8238841875801018,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.08351237517839771,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":6.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.008932302581448948,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":29.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.10916786422314964,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.02197870029715876,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":77.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0017237353259600483,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.08376,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":55.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Capitol Federal Financial, Inc. operates as the holding company for Capitol Federal Savings Bank that provides various retail banking products and services in the United States. The company offers a range of deposit products, including savings accounts, money market accounts, interest-bearing and non-interest-bearing checking accounts, and certificates of deposit, as well as retirement accounts. It also provides various loan products, such as one- to four-family residential real estate loans, commercial real estate, commercial and industrial, and construction loans, as well as consumer loans, which include home equity loans and lines of credit, home improvement loans, vehicle loans, and loans secured by savings deposits. In addition, the company offers mobile, telephone, and online banking services, as well as bill payment services and mortgage loan; operates a call center; and invests in various securities and mortgage-backed securities. Capitol Federal Financial, Inc. was founded in 1893 and is headquartered in Topeka, Kansas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John B. Dicus | CEO & Chairman | Age 64 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 622 people. Revenue per employee of $379K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $118K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $653 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Capitol Federal Financial, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $995M market cap on $236M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +137% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $74M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.93\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 17% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 51% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","26 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to CFFN Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/139/Technical_Reactions_to_CFFN_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_112526051401_1795601641.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795601641.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Capitol Federal Financial Inc. (CFFN) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/How_Capitol_Federal_Financial_Inc._CFFN_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111526070602_1794744362.html","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794744362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Capitol Federal Financial (CFFN) At 11.8x P E As Valuation Signals Split","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-cffn/capitol-federal-financial/news/capitol-federal-financial-cffn-at-118x-p-e-as-valuation-sign","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794731779.828,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Capitol Federal Financial (NASDAQ:CFFN) vs. Central Plains Bancshares (NASDAQ:CPBI) Head to Head Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/14/capitol-federal-financial-nasdaqcffn-vs-central-plains-bancshares-nasdaqcpbi-head-to-head-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794634135.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Capitol Federal Financial (CFFN) Looks Fully Valued On Fourth Quarter Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-cffn/capitol-federal-financial/news/capitol-federal-financial-cffn-looks-fully-valued-on-fourth","date":"2026-11-07","tim